, B8, B9(\u00d72): Already has chow potential [B6, B7, B8] and pair B9\n\n**Decision:**\nThe Chi action doesn't significantly improve my winning chances and would expose my hand, losing concealment bonuses. My current hand lacks a clear path to 8+ points even with the Chi. It's better to Pass and wait for better tiles to develop a higher-scoring hand.\n\nReason: Executing Chi W7 would expose a meld without creating a clear path to a winning hand with sufficient points (minimum 8 required). The remaining tiles after Chi would not form a valid winning structure. Passing maintains hand concealment for potential scoring bonuses and preserves flexibility to develop a better winning pattern.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
